-- title:
--   Geometric integrality of the generic fibre of the two-chart model
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be an arbitrary subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, let $p$ be a prime, and write $R =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) for the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator in lowest terms is coprime to $p$ (that is, $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$). Let $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ` be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set `intFormRatiosC ℚ Γ` of quotients $\iota(p_f)/\iota(p_g)$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of some common weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$, $\iota$ denotes the induced Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, and $\iota(p_g) \neq 0$. Let $j \in F$ be nonzero. Form the scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two maps $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the inclusions of the $R$-subalgebras `chartAlgFin` $=$ `chartAlg R F {j}` and `chartAlgInf` $=$ `chartAlg R F {j⁻¹}` of $F$ into the intermediate ring `XMid`, together with its structure morphism `TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,R$ induced by the two $R$-algebra structures. The assertion is that the second projection of the fibre product of this structure morphism with $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the inclusion $R \hookrightarrow \mathbb{Q}$, i.e. the generic fibre viewed as a scheme over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathbb{Q}$, is `GeometricallyIntegral`.
--
--   This is the characteristic-zero half of the integrality statement for the Kroneckerian model of a modular curve: the generic fibre of the two-chart model over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ attached to the field of modular functions for $\Gamma$ with rational $q$-expansions remains integral after any base field extension, no hypothesis relating $p$ to the level being imposed. It serves as the geometric-integrality ingredient of the Deligne–Rapoport style model data at $p$, and is used in the construction of level data representing relative sub-Picard schemes and in the production of Atkin–Lehner generic charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_geometricallyIntegral_pullback_snd_toBase_twoChartIntegralModel_qExpFunctionFieldC_rat.lean

